.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt BHOTKEYS-PANEL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bhotkeys-panel
.Nd chord list/editor for bhotkeys
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl greeter
.Op Bro Fl Fl enable | Fl Fl disable Brc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows each chord and edits whether it is on and what key runs it.
.Pp
With
.Fl Fl greeter
the list is read-only until the greeter unlock password is entered.
Combined with
.Fl Fl enable
or
.Fl Fl disable ,
.Fl Fl greeter
changes the greeter file instead of the session file.
That write requires the super-user.
.Pp
.Fl Fl disable
writes the session file so that neither the Panel chord nor the
Panel alt chord opens the list, and closes a list that is already
open.
No chord then opens the list, so a user cannot change chords or
turn them back on from the list.
It does not open the list.
Other lines in the file are left as they are.
.Pp
.Fl Fl enable
writes the session file so that the Panel chord and the Panel alt
chord open the list again.
It does not open the list.
Other lines in the file are left as they are.
.Pp
An unrecognized option prints the usage and exits non-zero.
.Pp
See
.Xr bhotkeys 1
for the list, the plugin file format, and the chords.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d"
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d
First directory of chord files.
.It Pa ~/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d
Second directory of chord files.
A file here replaces a system file with the same
.Li id .
.It Pa $BHOTKEYS_PLUGINS
Extra directory of chord files, scanned last.
A file here replaces the same
.Li id
from either directory above.
.It Pa ~/.config/bhotkeys/session
Saved checks, chords, and whether a chord opens the list.
When
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set, this file is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bhotkeys/session .
.It Pa ~/.config/bhotkeys/panel-ui
Saved sort and scroll.
Not read at the greeter.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bhotkeys/greeter
Greeter checks and chords. Lines have no window manager name.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bhotkeys.passwd
Greeter unlock hash.
See
.Xr bhotkeys-passwd 1 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys-passwd 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
